---
export const title = 'Usage';
export const order = 100;
import DemoComponentCard from '../../../../components/DemoComponentCard.astro';
---

<p>
  A toolbar groups related actions, such as formatting controls. Render the actions directly as
  children and separate groups with a vertical <code>wc-divider</code>. Give the toolbar an
  <code>aria-label</code> that names the group.
</p>

<DemoComponentCard lang={'html'}>
  <wc-toolbar aria-label='Formatting'>
    <wc-icon-button variant='text' color='surface' aria-label='Undo'><wc-icon name='undo'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>
    <wc-icon-button variant='text' color='surface' aria-label='Redo'><wc-icon name='redo'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>
    <wc-divider vertical></wc-divider>
    <wc-icon-button variant='tonal' aria-label='Bold'><wc-icon name='format_bold'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>
    <wc-icon-button variant='text' color='surface' aria-label='Italic'><wc-icon name='format_italic'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>
    <wc-icon-button variant='text' color='surface' aria-label='Underline'><wc-icon name='format_underlined'></wc-icon></wc-icon-button>
  </wc-toolbar>
</DemoComponentCard>

<br />

<h4 class='text-title'>Keyboard</h4>
<p>
  The toolbar is a single tab stop. Once focus is inside, the arrow keys along its orientation
  move between actions (Left and Right when horizontal, Up and Down when vertical), wrapping at
  the ends. <kbd>Home</kbd> and <kbd>End</kbd> jump to the first and last action. Disabled actions
  and dividers are skipped. The last focused action is where focus returns on the next
  <kbd>Tab</kbd>.
</p>
